The maintained LGPL source src/credule_brent.f90 translates that algorithm to
pure free-form Fortran with explicit reverse-communication state. The numerical
branches, interpolation conditions and machine-epsilon convergence rule are
retained. Bounds, nonfinite checks, exact endpoint handling and the iteration
limit are enforced by the MIT CDS caller. No callback with mutable global state
or embedded copy of another repository package is used.

The maintained CDS module, examples, tests and translation documentation carry
MIT notices. Mixed licensing is explicit in fpm.toml as
"MIT AND LGPL-2.1-or-later". Recipients of binaries linking the LGPL component
must observe the LGPL's applicable linking/relinking and source obligations.
The complete modified LGPL component is provided in source form here.

Dependency review: sibling rfortran-core supplies r_kinds:dp. The available
focused sibling libraries do not expose a compatible CDS or bracketed Brent
solver API. No shared dependency sources were copied or modified. No BLAS,
LAPACK, ARPACK, r.f90, r_mod.f90 or rfortran-compat is bundled or linked.
